// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: §2a [Str-Literal-View] (D-0134, D-0225): a literal, not a `str` binding; conf.str-binding-not-view-in-variant
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// Only a literal becomes a view where a variant's payload is a `StringView`
// (D-0225); a `str` binding is a value of type `str` and stays one, as for
// a parameter (D-0134): `Some(StringView::of(t))` is the form.
import std;

fn main()
{
    str t = "a str binding";
    Option<StringView> o = Some(t);
    printf("%v\n", Option::is_some(&o));
}
